=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
  ports ufw ----------------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Proposed: no Figma frame. web-01.example.net listens on 22, 80$
# and 443 on every address, 5353/udp, 5432 on loopback alone,$
# 9090 and 9100. ufw is active, denying by default, and lets in$
# 22, 80, 443 and 8080. The Ports section, after Rules: open,$
# blocked, local only, 8080, let in with nothing listening, and$
# 5353/udp, which ufw's own rules let in for mDNS alone.$
$
# UFW Firewall Configuration ###################################$
$
  [+] Firewall             + deny policy$
$
  ufw ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Installed            Yes$
  [+] Status               Active$
  [+] Incoming policy      Deny$
  [+] At boot              Yes$
$
  SSH ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] [::]:22              Allowed$
  [+] 0.0.0.0:22           Allowed$
$
  Rules --------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] 22/tcp               Allow$
  [+] 80/tcp               Allow$
  [+] 443/tcp              Allow$
  [+] 8080/tcp             Allow$
  [+] 22/tcp (v6)          Allow$
  [+] 80/tcp (v6)          Allow$
  [+] 443/tcp (v6)         Allow$
  [+] 8080/tcp (v6)        Allow$
$
  Ports --------------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  22/tcp               Open sshd$
   -  80/tcp               Open nginx$
   -  443/tcp              Open nginx$
   -  5353/udp             Some sources avahi-daemon$
   -  5432/tcp             Local only postgres$
  [ ] 8080/tcp             Open nothing listening$
   -  9090/tcp             Blocked prometheus$
   -  9100/tcp             Blocked node_exporter$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Disable firewall     Stop ufw (not recommended)$
   2) Application Profiles Add, remove, apply$
   3) Trusted Interfaces   Add, remove, apply$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Option [0-3 or q]:$
$
$

